CM k9ay_orig, trimmed to the cards the symmetric cell acts on (momwire#415).
CM Source: xnec2c examples/k9ay_orig.nec, a K9AY directional receiving loop.
CM Two wires meeting at (5, 0, 1.5); GX 2 100 reflects them in X=0, so the
CM cell is tags 1 and 2 and its image is tags 3 and 4.  EX drives tag 4 -- an
CM IMAGE -- and LD loads tag 2, which is inside the cell, so the 470 ohms
CM lands on tag 4 as well and the deck reads ~470 ohms higher than a naive
CM single-tag expansion would.  Free space and one frequency: the corpus
CM deck's Sommerfeld ground and 13-point sweep move both forms alike and are
CM not what this fixture is about.
CE
GW 1 8 0. 0. 8.5 5. 0. 1.5 1.5E-3
GW 2 5 0. 0. 0. 5. 0. 1.5 1.5E-3
GX 2 100
GE 0
EX 0 4 1 0 1. 0.
LD 4 2 1 1 470. 0.
FR 0 1 0 0 1.8 0
XQ
NX
